From: dandelion port <none@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] mediatek: stop selecting FW_LOADER_USER_HELPER_FALLBACK

The fallback turns a failed direct firmware load into a request handed to a
userspace helper over uevent, and then a 60 s wait for an answer. That design
belongs to Android, where ueventd answers it. NixOS runs no such helper, so on
this port every fallback is 60 s of a probe thread parked on a completion that
nothing will ever signal.

Two fire on a clean boot, for roughly 105 s of the boot spent blocking:

    t=32.77  Direct firmware load for WMT_STEP.cfg failed with error -2
    t=93.15  wmt_step_read_file: request_firmware failed          (60.4 s)

    t=28.02  Direct firmware load for novatek_ts_djn_fw.bin failed, error -2
    t=72.67  update_firmware_request 321: firmware load failed, ret=-11  (44.6 s)

The -11 in the second one is EAGAIN, which is what the helper path returns when
its timeout expires -- the tell that these are the fallback and not the direct
load, which had already failed 45 s earlier.

    drivers/misc/mediatek/Kconfig:1
        menuconfig MEDIATEK_SOLUTION
                bool "MediaTek Properitary Configuration"
                select FW_LOADER_USER_HELPER_FALLBACK

`select` is unconditional and bypasses `depends on`, so the symbol cannot be
turned off from a config file for as long as MEDIATEK_SOLUTION is set -- and
MEDIATEK_SOLUTION is the master switch for the whole platform, not something
this device can do without. Setting
`# CONFIG_FW_LOADER_USER_HELPER_FALLBACK is not set` in the defconfig is
silently reverted by `make oldconfig`; the line has to come out of the Kconfig.

FW_LOADER_USER_HELPER itself is left on. Only the fallback goes: request_firmware()
now fails immediately when the file is not on firmware_class.path, which is the
answer it was always going to arrive at.

--- a/drivers/misc/mediatek/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/misc/mediatek/Kconfig
@@ -1,6 +1,5 @@
 menuconfig MEDIATEK_SOLUTION
 	bool "MediaTek Properitary Configuration"
-	select FW_LOADER_USER_HELPER_FALLBACK
 	select I2C
 	help
 	  Check this to enable MediaTek properity configuration.
